NAME
       matchpathcon - show the default SELinux context for a path

SYNOPSIS
       matchpathcon [-V] PATH...

DESCRIPTION
       matchpathcon prints the context the SELinux policy (including your
       semanage fcontext rules) gives each PATH, which is the context
       restorecon would set. The path does not have to exist.

OPTIONS
       -V     Verify: compare the file's real context with the default and
              say "verified" or what it should be.

EXAMPLES
           matchpathcon /var/www/html/index.html
           matchpathcon -V /srv/web/index.html

SEE ALSO
       restorecon(8), semanage(8), ls(1)
